e_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.07679863209152996,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":7.7,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.041613023842049734,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":8.4,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.010940818937218454,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":23.3,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00159,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Centerra Gold Inc. engages in the operation, development, exploration, and acquisition of gold and copper properties in North America, Turkey, and internationally. The company also owns and operates a molybdenum business unit, which includes a metallurgical processing facility and two primary molybdenum properties. The company was incorporated in 2002 and is headquartered in Toronto, Canada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Paul Botond Stilicho Tomory | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Centerra Gold Inc. is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $3.9B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are contracting by -17.7pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $160M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -17.7pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 78% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7826770409048225},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 57/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 52% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Among the least levered in Basic Materials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with Centerra Gold Inc. (CGAU) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/14/Precision_Trading_with_Centerra_Gold_Inc._CGAU_Risk_Zones_110526035801_1793869081.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793869081.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Centerra Gold Inc. (NYSE:CGAU) Stock Has Consensus Price Target of $21.00 According to Brokerages","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/centerra-gold-inc-nysecgau-stock-has-consensus-price-target-of-21-00-according-to-brokerages-2.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793789944.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Why Are Record Share Repurchases Putting Centerra Gold (NYSE:CGAU) in the Spotlight?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/gold/why-are-record-share-repurchases-putting-centerra-gold-nysecgau-in-the-spotlight","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793699160.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.758,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Bear of the Day: Centerra Gold (CGAU)","source":"